\f0\fs24 \cf0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs26 \'93Resources have their limits, Mr Prime Minister.\'94 \
\'93Mr President, two million foreign troops have foothold on our soil, occupying our gold fields, uranium mines and iron ore deposits, plundering our resources.\'94\
Dunning-Kruger pursed his lips in an excessively sensual pout and shrugged.\
\'93Our economy will be ruined,\'94 Muddleham said, as if explaining the alphabet to a child. We will not be able to pay off our loans, Mr President.\'94 He knew this would get his attention. Although they habitually neglected to pay their own bills, holding fast to belief in their exceptionalism, Atlantians despised states that did not pay their bills. \
\'93You guys owe us 3 trillion as it is.\'94 Kruger, soft as his head was, did not like to be stiffed.\
\'93This is an intolerable situation and we do not have the resources to repel them. Our great peoples have fought and died alongside each other for close to two centuries. Where is your sense of history? Where is your sense of honour?\'94\
Raising the concept of \'93honour\'94 in diplomacy struck Kruger as immensely amusing and he could barely choke down the urge to laugh hysterically. SecDef and Sec State were not able to display the same degree of self-discipline and spent the next several minutes cackling on the floor. \
When he was finally able, the President choked out, \'93Honour costs money. I can\'92t afford honour. Honour is the rallying cry of losers. As for history, we make history. We are not slaves to it. Any history we do not like, we re-write. In any case, where are your defence forces, Mr Prime Minister?\'94 \
\'93Well, Mr President, most of them are fighting anti-Semites, in all ten theaters \'94 
\f2\i Don\'92t you remember? You fucking idiot!
\f1\i0 \
\'93You\'92ve only given us one million of your troops \'96 where are the rest?\'94 Inquired the ignoramus.\
\'93That\'92s pretty much it. We\'92ve got reservists and retirees, but no front line troops. Relocating troops currently deployed will take time. Time is something we do not have.\'94\
\'93You sent all of your troops offshore? Are you insane?\'94 Questioned the inane President.\
\'93It was in response to your \'91Plea to the Free World\'92 speech \'96 you know, \'91If you\'92re not with us you\'92re against us\'92. It scared the shit out of us. We asked how many and you said one million, no less.\'94\
President Kruger was pleased. 
\f2\i Fear is power!
\f1\i0  He loved the idea of scaring the entire planet with a one-liner. He\'92d have to promote his speech writer - 
\f2\i If you\'92re not with us you\'92re against us. 
\f1\i0 He giggled again. \'93It was supposed to scare you into action. We seem to be the only defender of freedom and democracy on this planet.\'94\
\'93We have been alongside you all of the way.\'94\
\'93You\'92re contribution is token at best, Prime Minister. We pay the bills.\'94\
\'93Yeah and you take all the loot.\'94\
 \'93Yes, we do. What do these people want anyway? Free Trade? A seat on the League of Nations Security Council? Cheaper loans? What?\'94 Asked the President, directing the conversation away from his country\'92s well-documented history of pillaging and plundering.\
 \
\'93They say they are running war-games, but they mostly want to punish us for intellectual property infringements. They say they want us to change the way we do business. They want free trade agreements to be adhered to.\'94\
\'93Agreements adhered to? Don\'92t you guys know how to write an exit clause? If we can\'92t renege on a deal, we don\'92t sign.\'94 
\f2\i These Ulyssians are like children. No wonder their economy sucks
\f1\i0 .\
\'93It\'92s also a good excuse to steal our gold, uranium and iron ore. While we sit on our backsides, they are stealing my country. They\'92re just thieves like the rest of us and we cannot ignore them or their demands. Basically they want, you know, fair and equitable treatment in the future.\'94 \
Fair and equitable treatment between trading partners was an alien concept to those involved in commerce. It was inconceivable to build an economic powerhouse on evenhanded treatment of others. Taking advantage of weaker nations was (and is) the foundation of international business. A high living standard for a few in one location, by definition, insists that there are low standards for many somewhere else. Those suckers dumb enough to be born in poor nations deserve exploitation, and by remaining vulnerable, invite yet more exploitation. It was simply a fact of life.\
Dunning Kruger found himself entirely bemused at the nativity of the Vietnesians. 
\f2\i Are they that unsophisticated? 
\f1\i0 \'93Mr Prime Minister, I am told by my Defence Secretary that there may be something we can do for you. I don\'92t have all the details yet, I\'92ll get back to you as soon as I have them. It will comply with our obligations under the Nuclear Disarmament Treaty, but, whatever happens, however, there will be no troops sent from here\'94 \
\'93I don\'92t care about details. If you can help, just do it.\'94 He hung up the phone and breathed a sigh of relief. Scratched his head and then stopped dead in his tracks. Huh? 
\f2\i Nuclear Disarmament Treaty?
\f1\i0 \
Twenty-seven minutes later, in excess of 100 nuclear missiles air-burst over the Vietnesian positions and in the following ten microseconds two million Vietnesians were vaporized into plasma smoke and radioactive gas. In the process, 80% of arable land in Western Ulyssia was annihilated. After irradiating the entire mineral reserves of a small continent, President Kruger called it a good day, lit a cigar and poured himself a scotch. Nothing was left of the invasion and nothing much was left of the countryside. A glowing moonscape was left to fester and expand. There was nothing worth invading now.\
- - -\
\'93Jesus Christ, Dunning, what the hell did you think you were doing? Nuking my country!\'94 A somewhat irate Prime Minister screamed down the hot line. \
\'93You said and I quote \'96 \'91I don\'92t care about details. If you can help, just do it.\'92 I have it recorded. Turn on your vid-screen, it\'92s on 
\f2\i WWNN
\f1\i0  right now,\'94 he replied, barely able to stop himself from laughing. The Defence Secretary and the National Security adviser were again on the floor, wetting themselves. No end of amusement at that end of the phone.\
\'93Did you seriously think that this would help?\'94 queried the PM.\
\'93We had to do something about complying with our Nuclear Disarmament Treaty. We had to dismantle them, so we figured we might as well deploy them.\'94\
\'93How does that comply with the fucking treaty? You are supposed to dismantle them!\'94\
\'93I dismantled them very quickly and into many, many small pieces. What are you complaining about anyway? Do you currently have an invading army on your doorstep?\'94\
\'93No, but half of my country glows in the dark.\'94\
\'93Be that as it may, those nukes come at a price. Your little shit-hole country owes the Union of Capitalist Atlantic States 6 trillion. In Atlantian dollars, not your southern fucking pesos! There is no need to thank us, just pay up. While you are at it you can pay the 3 trillion you already owe.\'94 \
\'93What will you do if we don\'92t pay? Nuke us?\'94\
\'93Our response will be proportionate to your debt.\'94 He knew this would frighten him. He had wiped out entire countries for less.\
\'93You\'92ll get your money. You\'92ll get your money.\'94 Even as he terminated the call, the PM knew his career was over. Nothing could save him now. He\'92d be lucky to live until the next election and he knew was not that lucky.\
Dunning and the crew were now backslapping and congratulating each other. Another customer satisfied and another diplomatic crisis solved. \'93Man, one day we are going to have to take this shit seriously!\'94 Teased the president. \
\'93Nine trillion in one day. The treasury is going to love you, Mr. President. Yours will be remembered as the most fiscally responsible administration in history. Your policies are epoch making,\'94 said SecDef, sucking up to the chief.\
\'93Do you ever stop brown-nosing? For the last time, you will not get the nomination next term.\'94\
\'93Oh, but..\'94\
\'93No buts. There is no way this country is ever going to vote for President Mohamed Goldberg. Go plan your next war.\'94 He pointed to the door and both of the cabinet members left. \'93Everyone wants my job. Now, I wonder if they will really pay up.\'94 
\f2\i Epoch making? What the hell does that mean?
\f1\i0 \
Pay up they did. It amused the Prime Minister to deliver the payment in gold bullion, all from the glowing west, radioactive and useless for several hundred thousand years. \
Following the nuclear strike on their lands, the Provincial Government of Western Ulyssia withdrew from the Federation and called the new land the Western Liberated Dominion. It sounded pretty cool, but the Western Liberated Dominion was nothing more than a nuclear landfill with a couple of unaffected cities. They would never be an economic force again. They could have their pathetic little Nation-State. No one in the east cared.\
The political ramifications for the PM were ugly and immediate. Outraged citizens and their pitiful street demonstrations were simply ignored, but the corporate sector could not be so readily disregarded. Any company that owned businesses in the Western Liberated Dominion, were screaming for blood. The Prime Minister\'92s political stocks plummeted and the party invoked a time honoured tradition of assassination \'96 stabbed to death in the chamber of the lower house. As he lay dying he could not help but think of Caesar. Parallel lives, he ridiculously thought. With his last breath he wheezed, \'93
\f2\i Et tu Brute?
\f1\i0 \'94 \
The new Prime Minister stood over the body and mocked, \'93
\f2\i Et tu, Brute?
\f1\i0  Et tu, Fucking Brute! Who the fuck did he think he was?\'94 Slamming his boot into the emotionless death mask he said, \'93Oh well, at least he didn\'92t say \'91Rosebud\'92.\'94 Some of the older party members were mildly amused, but others could not place the reference, being more concerned with how they were going to get the blood off their shoes before the press conference.\
Riding on a wave of anti-Atlantian sentiment, the new regime became tough, adopting an isolationist policy, combining the geniality of communist regimes with the human compassion of a military junta. Ulyssia, a country now split in two, was renamed the Primary Trade Dominion and the economy, previously based upon consumer goods and service industries, would now focus on the manufacture of arms. How hard could it be to sell weapons? Any idiot could do it. The trick was staying under the radar so you could sell to all sides in a conflict. Better still, create the conflict, having first arranged the contracts. Everyone else sold weapons that way and everyone knew it, but it was bad form to be caught unloading them, particularly when the recipient is an enemy of an ally. It was \ul the\ulnone  biggest market and needing money desperately, the PTD became the most prosperous war-monger in history. They sold to anyone and everyone and siphoned up cash from all comers.\
It took only a few short years for the radiation zone in the Western Liberated Dominion to expand and engulf urban centres. Terrified citizens fled to the east, to where it was said to be safe from the rads. There were millions of them, mostly from the Western Liberated Dominion, but a few malformed Vietnesians made the trek as well. They had escaped the radiation storms with nothing but their lives and a few meagre possessions. Any prior land ownership was meaningless. The wealth they had created and the trinkets they had owned were now throbbing with radioactive isotopes of iodine, caesium, strontium, thorium, xenon and barium.\
As the trickle of radioactive refugees became a flood, PTD cities began to bulge and then burst from the pressure. The wretched throngs kept coming in massive human waves, ever-increasing, laying wast to vast areas of urban sprawl. The only saleable resource they possessed was their labour, gleefully exploited by local business, happy to see the return of slavery. The workers were used, abused and discarded. In traditional blue-collar work there were no protective labour laws and no benefits. 
\f2\i Thanks for coming, champ. Sorry about the severed limb, but we do have a two-arm policy here. I think you will find the exit is behind you.
\f1\i0 \
There were a few benevolent souls who, against all good sense, actually assisted the refugees. One stood out head and shoulders above the rest. Jameson Hardy was the wealthiest man in all of Old Ulyssia (some said the world), but to his peers, he was the most eccentric of men. Had he been poor, he would have been merely regarded as insane, but he controlled the finance and resources sector, manufacturing, media, ship yards, universities, hospitals, pharmaceuticals, schools, utilities, multi-national conglomerates and, much to the amusement of the boys at "The Club", he also delved in charitable foundations, training schemes and general tree-hugging, hippy non-sense. Of course, there were hardly any trees left to hug, but the term was now synonymous with any unworthy left wing activity. \
He poured obscene amounts of money into apparently useless research. His interest in things medical was peculiar in that it was focused on epidemiology and genetic diversity amongst \'93the common\'94, level 1 and level 2 citizens. 
\f2\i Very strange indeed - Who cares if \'93the common\'94 get Ebola? Who cares if they are all inbred? They need to be culled back a bit anyway
\f1\i0 . \
All in all, Jamison Hardy was an oddity, some sort of throwback, who somehow came to the conclusion that helping others enriched your life. 
\f2\i What was he playing at? Where was the profit? Can you still claim that sort of thing on tax? 
\f1\i0 In fact there was no profit in helping innocent victims of war. Jameson Hardy knew he would never get a return on this investment. Apparently, shocking as it seemed, he was on a humanitarian mission. He was a Dutch boy inserting his digit into a dyke holding back a deluge of human misery. He knew that eventually the walls would fail and a flood of pain would follow. Fatalistic or not, he was going to relieve the suffering of as many as he could before cataclysm engulfed them. He purchased, from the filthy throngs, every parcel of land he could. He purchased millions of hectares - all radioactive and uninhabitable. While the vendors were eternally grateful for the money, it was insufficient to purchase comparable lodgings in the swelling metropolis. Demand for housing far-outstretched supply, causing a price surge. Anyone with a proprietary interest in land rubbed their hands together with delight.\
Jameson embarked upon unprecedented building programs employing hundreds of thousands of workers, refugees all. Toiling against time, they constructed housing estates, hundreds of stories tall, with Spartan, but clean facilities. Each gargantuan structure was designed to house 30,000, but eventually squeezed in 100,000 with the introduction of time share and sleeping drawers. \
The popularity of time-share, the equivalent of camping in the city, was astonishing. Some chose to time-share an entire house or flat for a fixed period (up to 6 months), preferring to spend an equivalent time on the streets rather than permanently living in a drawer. Although they were not officially called drawers, "Discreet Living Capsules" were nothing more than suffocating coffins. They were relatively cheap and provided security when in repose, but sharing bathroom facilities necessarily involved running the gauntlet through a permanent gaggle of rapists and paedophiles. They were harmless compared to \'91Gazumpers\'92 who would perpetually circulate dorms looking for unlocked drawers, hoping to spend a few unconscious hours in comfort and at someone else's expense. These people rarely had the opportunity to bath and being gazumped meant disinfecting the whole drawer, including the bedding and any personal other items that were, for some reason, not stolen.\
Forlorn home-owners riddled with debt, sold off or leased 8 to 12 hours access a day to their humble abodes. Usually shift workers would take the opportunity to get a few hours\'92 sleep, a meal and a shower before going back to the grind. These marriages of convenience were the source of a great deal of unrest, but in stark contrast to life on the streets, disputes rarely ended in death or loss of limb. In the ultimate housing boom, housing sales management became a most lucrative vocation and owning an Accommodation Directorate franchise was comparable to printing money. Realtors joined the new elite and property ownership became the symbol of social status and power. \
When the plague came Jameson Hardy disappeared, presumed dead. The refugees from the west mourned his death loud and long. Many had been given the chance to grow into adults, some of which did not live entirely miserable lives. The evil epidemic, which was said to have come from Asia (most suspected Vietnesia) was swift, smiting 40% of the population before the disease and the rioting dissipated. Even though it could be proven the bug was a genetically modified virus, the plague was blamed on the immigrants in Jameson Hardy's towering cesspools. \
Although a huge swath of the population had been cut down, there were still plenty of street-sleepers and gazumpers to go around. In fact, a disproportionate amount of \'93the common\'94 had survived the plague. Was it luck or natural immunity? Very odd, indeed, but no-one bothered to find out why this was so. 
\f2\i Fuck the poor.
\f1\i0 \
The property owners and accommodation directorates got down to the business of perpetuating a housing crisis. Real Estate moguls properly thanked a non-existent god that there was still enough demand to apply upward pressure on prices. Many apartment blocks were destroyed or condemned in order to maintain a shortage. People could go ahead and die en-masse, but property values could not fall.\

